# All HNS hostnames route through the Bun gateway (127.0.0.1:4049), which owns
# routing: app.<root>/apex -> app origin, api.<root> -> API origin, usernames ->
# public profile pages, other reserved hosts -> 404, and ANY other hostname ->
# dynamic /public-namespaces/:root resolution. Keeping routing in the gateway
# (tested code) instead of proxy config means the catchall genuinely covers
# arbitrary community roots.
#
# The gateway injects x-pirate-hns-host and the forwarder token itself
# (HNS_PUBLIC_FORWARDER_AUTH_TOKEN in its env) — do not add header_up overrides
# for those here.
#
# HTTPS for HNS names cannot use ACME (no ICANN CA). `tls internal` with
# on-demand issuance serves per-host certs signed by Caddy's local CA; publish
# matching DANE-EE TLSA records (and DS-anchored DNSSEC) for clients that
# validate DANE. Plain HTTP stays available for HNS clients without DANE
# support — non-canonical origins are public/read-only in the app
# (web/docs/auth-origin-spec.md), so no credentials ride over it.

{
  local_certs
}

https:// {
  tls internal {
    on_demand
  }
  reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4049
}

http:// {
  reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:4049
}
